  "selection": "Seventeen cover observations. The triangle carries the three singleton blocks, one overlapping pair of blocks, and three partial covers that each omit one edge. The four-cycle carries the two blocks of opposite edges. The laws are the empty list and one multiply by 3 of edge (0,1) when edge (1,2) is present. The bare intersection of the singleton blocks is the edge-count label. Its empty-list cell is the atlas-008 triangle count and is not repeated. The four-edge path is not a carrier. The bit covers of the path fixture are not repeated. A nested cover is not a cell. Not scheduled to explain the path-cover defects, the atlas-010 defects, PAT-013, EQ-020, EQ-021, EQ-022, or EQ-023. EQ-021 is the empty-list edge-count identity. The constrained bare cell lies outside it. A comparison of the triangle with the four-cycle is joint with the placement of the designated pair. The three omissions share the triangle and the law. They differ by which edge the cover leaves out.",
  "grammar": {
